- add the subject's projected bounding box and the bar as obstacles;
- prefer 'above' or 'left' with a leader line.

Water shader reads as a 'swimming pool': neon turquoise to the horizon over banks 20-60 m deep (regions_check nihoa, gardner, kure, lalo), and a flat, textureless cyan sheet over 50% of the frame at close range (final_holei, final_halape). Fix:
- ramp the depth colour to deep blue by about 25 m;
- add wave normals and sun glint;
- add a surf/foam band at the shoreline.
The same ramp makes f000419-f000637 less cyan.

The STORY globe (toolkit/globe_story_f90.jpg) fails several rules:
- luma 79;
- the Big Island hero is about 110 px wide, under the 120 px floor and far from a third of the width;
- the HAWAIʻI plate covers the other islands' outlines;
- blocky 8-16 px texture artefacts at bottom centre, x 800-900, y 930-1050 (review_vis/globe_blocks.jpg);
- glowing cyan smears in the cloud and shelf layer.

Fix:
- lower the altitude so the chain fills at least a third of the width;
- exposure +0.5 stop;
- treat outlines as obstacles for the label placer;
- run the high-pass seam check, and fix the cloud seam near 160 W.

The terrain-to-globe crossfade (xfade f66) ghosts the incoming globe's HAWAIʻI label at 50% over the terrain, and dissolves between two very different scales. Fix:
- draw the incoming shot's UI only after the dissolve ends;
- for scale jumps, prefer the look book's S14 move (log-altitude zoom from space to place over 3-5 s), or a match-cut at the same lon/lat/heading.

Paper kit draft (toolkit/paper_postcard_standee_draft_f45.jpg):
- the standee stands on a grey slab base and has no contact shadow;
- the postcard's HAWAIʻI is about 30 px cap, too small to read on a phone;
- in Anton the ʻokina renders as a mid-dot or hyphen (review_vis/postcard_okina.jpg). Use U+2018, or Barlow, and check glyph coverage in T.width.

Also, the postcard face is our own drained render. It must be a real public-domain photo, per s003.

